<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN JAN NEW CAR SALES UP 13.5 PERCENT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN JAN NEW CAR SALES UP 13.5 PERCENT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African new car sales</p>
<p>rose 13.5 percent to 19,831 units in January compared to 17,477</p>
<p>units in the same month a year ago and 17,681 in December last</p>
<p>year, latest National Association of Automobile Manufacturers of</p>
<p>South Africa figures show.</p>
<p>    Detailed Sales data:	 Jan 97   Dec 96  Jan 96 </p>
<p>    New passenger cars	   19,831   17,681  17,477</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles   7,967    8,367  10,021</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles    382	346     282</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles     416	502     600</p>
<p>    TOTAL:			   28,596   26,896  28,380</p>
<p>Individual manufacturer car sales:</p>
<p>Toyota 6,483, Volkswagen 5,462, Samcor 4,479, Nissan 2,613,</p>
<p>Delta 4,840, Mercedes-Benz 2,729, BMW 1,019, Land Rover SA 205,</p>
<p>Daewoo 471, Iveco 68, Tyco 55, MAN 43, Dacia 1, Erf 8, AAD 19,</p>
<p>Scania 6, Subaru 7, Freightliner 15.</p>
<p>					    Jan-Dec 96   Jan-Dec 95 </p>
<p>    New passenger cars		249,884	 236,584</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles     129,575	 128,397 </p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles	5,457	   4,139</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles	 8,110	   7,664</p>
<p>    TOTAL:				393,026	 376,784</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
